WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.300
In a time of social division, we often
hear about how politics drives us apart.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.650
But we never really hear about what
brings us together. Well, it turns out

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:18.020
some pretty simple things can help, like
living in a community rich in amenities

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:25.320
such as grocery stores, parks, libraries,
bars and restaurants — even gyms! A recent

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.130
AEI survey finds that people who live
within a walking distance or a short

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:32.669
drive from a grocery store, park, or
favorite restaurant know their neighbors

00:00:32.669 --> 00:00:37.260
better than people who live farther out.
People who live close to their favorite

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.430
bar or restaurant, gym, or theater are
much more likely to rate their community

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:46.460
an excellent place to live than people
who have to drive more than 15 minutes.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.520
57% of people who walk to their grocery
store talk to their neighbors several

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.930
times a week, compared to just 42% of
those who have to drive more than 15

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:59.460
minutes. Now, it may not be a panacea, but
where we live and how we design our

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.300
communities might just be a good first
step toward hating each other less and

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.180
maybe learning to get along a little bit more.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.140
What about your community do you like most?

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:13.080
Let us know in your comments.
Also, let us know what other topics you'd

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.070
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,
and be sure to like and subscribe for

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.689
more research and videos from AEI.

